TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes on **hook methods** (which must be static), plus `[BeforeEvery(…)]` / `[AfterEvery(…)]` for global hooks. Here's a sketch for each scope:

---

### 1. Before/After every individual test in a class

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public static async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs before each test in this class
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public static async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs after each test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task MyTest() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before/after the class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client = new HttpClient();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task CallsApi() { /* use _client */ }
}
```

---

### 3. Once before/after the assembly

Place these in **any class** in the assembly (commonly a dedicated hooks class):

```csharp
public class GlobalHooks
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start WireMock once for the whole assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // tear down WireMock
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

Use `[BeforeEvery(TestSession)]` / `[AfterEvery(TestSession)]`:

```csharp
public class SessionHooks
{
    [BeforeEvery(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [AfterEvery(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick reference

| Scope | Attribute | Context parameter | Where |
|-------|-----------|-------------------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | `TestContext` | In the test class |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `ClassHookContext` | In the test class |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `AssemblyHookContext` | Any class in assembly |
| Session | `[BeforeEvery(TestSession)]` / `[AfterEvery(TestSession)]` | `TestSessionContext` | Any class in assembly |

All hook methods must be **`static`** (and can be `async Task`). The `HookType` enum values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) are imported via `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;`.
